# Wave W17-Y (Route 213): rack post — a painted-boat rack post along the shore: two posts and a crossbar carrying one small painted hull, teal over red, the beachcomber’s boats kept off the wet sand (design: boats on racks all along the shore under the hotels). On salt turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s single posts by the rack entire: a post marks a place, a rack keeps a boat.
